# Trivy deploy-gate suppressions (read automatically by the trivy-action in
# deploy.yml — "Trivy gate (CRITICAL,HIGH; fail closed)").
#
# Each entry is a DOCUMENTED, time-boxed risk-acceptance, not a "fix". Remove the
# entry as soon as the underlying dependency can be patched.
#
# ── multer 2.1.1 Denial-of-Service advisories ───────────────────────────────
# The patch is multer 2.2.0, but @nestjs/platform-express pins multer EXACTLY
# 2.1.1 (even in its latest release, 11.1.27) and npm 11.9.0 silently refuses to
# apply an `overrides` bump, so the version cannot be raised cleanly yet.
#
# Risk is mitigated and LOW in context:
#   - the only code paths that reach multer are the image-upload endpoints,
#   - which are AUTH-GATED (vendor/admin only),
#   - RATE-LIMITED (RATE_LIMIT_CALLBACK, 20/min/IP) behind Cloudflare,
#   - fileSize-capped (10 MB), and
#   - fields/parts/fieldNameSize-capped (PR #385) — which closes the
#     "deeply nested field names" DoS vector at the app layer.
#
# REMOVE these once NestJS ships a @nestjs/platform-express that depends on a
# patched multer (Dependabot will open that PR). Tracked in the project memory
# note `reference_deploy_trivy_gate`.
CVE-2026-5079
GHSA-72gw-mp4g-v24j
GHSA-3p4h-7m6x-2hcm

# ── sharp 0.34.5 — inherited libvips advisories ─────────────────────────────
# Review by: 2026-09-30
#
# The patch is sharp >= 0.35.0, but it CANNOT be applied in isolation: `next`
# depends on sharp@^0.34.3, so bumping only apps/api installs 0.35.x nested
# while npm keeps the vulnerable 0.34.5 hoisted at the root — the image ends up
# carrying BOTH copies and the finding does not clear. Verified by attempting
# the bump: it produced a duplicate sharp and a 669-line lockfile diff, so it
# was reverted. A root `overrides` forcing sharp across next is possible but
# sharp/libvips is the exact package behind this project's past non-
# deterministic deploy failures, so it needs its own PR with a build test.
#
# Risk is mitigated and LOW in context — every claim below was verified in code:
#   - sharp is reached from exactly ONE place, apps/api/src/common/services/
#     upload.service.ts:8 (only import in the repo),
#   - via image-upload endpoints that are AUTH-GATED: admin.controller.ts is
#     class-level @UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard) + @Roles('ADMIN'), and
#     vendor.controller.ts:269 upload-image is @Roles('VENDOR','ADMIN'),
#   - RATE-LIMITED (@Throttle(RATE_LIMIT_CALLBACK), 20/min/IP) behind Cloudflare,
#   - fileSize-capped (upload.service.ts:242), and
#   - content-sniffed with `file-type` fileTypeFromBuffer BEFORE processing, so
#     a non-image payload is rejected before it reaches libvips.
# Exploiting these requires an authenticated vendor/admin uploading a crafted
# image within those limits — not an anonymous internet-facing vector.
#
# REMOVE when the next 15 -> 16 upgrade lands (next 16 allows sharp 0.35), or
# when a reviewed root override ships. Tracked alongside the same advisory in
# .audit-allowlist.json (GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj), which must be removed together.
GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj
CVE-2026-33327
CVE-2026-33328
CVE-2026-35590
CVE-2026-35591

# ── postcss 8.4.31 — vendored INSIDE next, pinned exactly ───────────────────
# Review by: 2026-09-30
#
# This is NOT our postcss. The root dependency is already patched (8.5.10 at
# node_modules/postcss, plus an `overrides` entry). The flagged copy lives at
# node_modules/next/node_modules/postcss because next 15.5.23 declares
# `"postcss": "8.4.31"` — an EXACT pin, not a range. Verified empirically: a
# root `overrides` bump does NOT dislodge it (npm refuses against an exact
# pin, same wall as the multer entry above). Only upgrading next fixes it, and
# the fix version is next 16.3.1 — a major upgrade that needs its own tested PR.
#
# Risk is LOW in context — verified against the actual runner image contents:
#   - postcss is a BUILD-TIME CSS transformer. The web runner stage copies only
#     .next/standalone + .next/static + public (apps/web/Dockerfile, runner
#     stage) and starts `node server.js`, serving CSS that was already compiled
#     during the build.
#   - No request path invokes postcss at runtime; Trivy is reporting the
#     presence of a package.json manifest traced into the standalone output,
#     not executing code.
#   - The advisories are ReDoS/parsing issues that require attacker-controlled
#     CSS to be parsed — we never parse untrusted CSS at runtime.
#
# REMOVE together with the sharp block above when next 15 -> 16 lands. Tracked
# alongside the same advisories in .audit-allowlist.json, which must be
# cleaned up in the same PR.
CVE-2026-45623
